error[type]: this call of `chained` takes a frame for every round
 --> shape__a_plain_alias_is_what_it_names.silt:12:7
    |
 12 |   1 + again(n + 1)
    |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^ this call of `chained` takes a frame for every round
  = note: not the last thing `chained` does, and `n + 1` is not a part of `n`
  = note: `again` is `chained`: an alias is the function it names
  = help: carry the running value in a parameter, so that the call comes last
  = help: if its depth is bounded by something the compiler cannot see, write `deep fn chained`

